Agile Team Charter 
1. Team Purpose & Vision 
Why do we exist as a team? We exist to design and deliver a viable community-focused 
business solution that addresses the critical sanitation crisis in Khayelitsha, Cape town.  
Team Mission: 
• We are solving the problem of frequent sewage pipe bursts and blocked drains in 
Khayelitsha townships. These failures leave residents – including households, schools, 
and small businesses-without clean water for cooking, drinking and hygiene, sometimes 
for multiple days at a time. Our solution serves the residents of Khayelitsha and the 
surrounding municipality.  
Success Definition:  
We will know we are successful when: 
• Our business idea is clearly defined, researched, and supported by community survey 
data 
• The value proposition addresses the real problem experienced by Khayelitsha residents 
• All team members have contributed to their assigned roles and deliverables 
• The final report and presentation are submitted on time and meet the assignment rubric 
• Our proposed service demonstrates a credible path to reducing sewage incidents and 
improving sanitation 
Product / Service 
We are responsible for delivering a comprehensive community business proposal for a Sewage 
Repair & Monitoring service in Khayelitsha. This includes community research and surveys, a 
defines business model, a value proposition, and a professional presentation of findings. 
