9. Risks & Constraints 
What could impact our success? 
Known Risks 
• Team members may have conflicting academic schedules or part-time work commitments 
• Internet connectivity and data access may limit participation in virtual meetings 
• Survey response rates from Khayelitsha community members may be low 
• Limited practical experience in business planning may affect depth of proposals 
Dependencies 
• Access to community surveys and responses via Google Forms 
• Availability of credible sources on Khayelitsha sanitation infrastructure 
• Timely feedback from the lecturer on draft submissions 
• Municipality and infrastructure data to support the business case 
Constraints 
• Time: Academic deadlines are fixed; the project must be completed within the semester 
• Budget: No financial resources – all tools used are free (Google Drive, Trello, WhatsApp, Google Meet) 
• Tools: Limited to tools accessible to all team members without cost 
• Skills: Team members are students with varying levels of business and technical knowledge 
